      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note: Please read my comment in vpx/src/vpx_image.c first.\n\nLines 67 - 71 show that this test expects the flip and set_rect operations are commutative. In general we cannot assume two operations are commutative. For example, in mathematics courses we learned that function composition is not commutative and matrix multiplication is not commutative.\n\nHere is an example from C++ coding that captures the essence of the problem. Consider the byteswap and low16 operations defined as follows:\n\nbyteswap: swaps the byte order of the input integer (32-bit or 16-bit)\n\nlow16: returns the least significant 16 bits of the input integer (32-bit).\n\nThese two operations are not commutative.\n\n```\nlow16( byteswap\u003cuint32_t\u003e(0x12345678) ) \u003d low16(0x87654321) \u003d 0x4321\n\nbyteswap\u003cuint16_t\u003e( low16(0x12345678) ) \u003d byteswap\u003cuint16_t\u003e(0x5678) \u003d 0x8765\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "01a78fbc3b25c6a9eb227973bd591e9092d6daa1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
